<title>USA: WHX sees Q4 loss due to steel plant strike.</title>
<headline>WHX sees Q4 loss due to steel plant strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>WHX Corp said on Friday it expected to report a material loss in the fourth quarter because of strikes at several of its steel production and finishing facilities in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Virginia.</p>
<p>The United Steelworkers of America union began a strike on October 1 and was picketing eight facilities, WHX said.</p>
<p>No steel products were being produced or shipped at the eight facilities, it said.</p>
<p>WHX said its labor agreement with the union expired on October 1. It said about 70 percent of its workforce is covered by the collective bargaining agreement.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
